      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please do not give your 7-year-old aspirin, as it can cause Reye's syndrome, which is very serious in children. Instead, use children's acetaminophen (Tylenol) or ibuprofen (Motrin/Advil) appropriate for his weight and age to help manage the fever and discomfort. If his fussiness or headache worsens, or if you are worried, it is best to contact your pediatrician or an after-hours nurse line for advice.",
